= Two Senators

Our majority in the Senate is 50 plus the Vice President. Two moderate Democratic senators block the more ambitious plans and refuse to change the filibuster. Activists threaten primaries. The Senate calendar slips.

- @infra: Pass the bipartisan infrastructure bill first.
- @hold: Hold the infrastructure bill hostage.
- @filibuster: Push for filibuster reform on voting rights.

@infra
subtitle: A win.
on-arrival: pop_mod += 0.3; enthusiasm -= 1; prog_dissent += 3; mod_dissent -= 3

The infrastructure bill passes with Republican votes. The larger social package stalls.

@hold
subtitle: Leverage.
on-arrival: prog_dissent -= 2; mod_dissent += 3; unity -= 2; capital -= 1 if capital > 0

Hardball. It does not move the two senators.

@filibuster
subtitle: Principle.
on-arrival: voting_rights += 1; stability += 2; enthusiasm += 2; mod_dissent += 2; capital -= 1 if capital > 0

The effort fails when two senators refuse to go along. The voting-rights bills die.
